unks":[{"i":0,"s":0,"e":520.49,"state":"done"}]},"artifacts":{"summary":{"text":"Roosevelt asks Congress to declare war on Japan the morning after Pearl Harbor, opening with the sentence that named the day: December 7th, 1941, \"a date which will live in infamy\" [1]. The speech is built like a legal case: the distance of Hawaii from Japan proves the attack was planned days or weeks in advance [2], while Japan's diplomats were still talking peace — a deliberate deception [3].\n\nThe evidence lands as a drumbeat of overnight attacks across the Pacific — Malaya, Hong Kong, Guam, the Philippines, Wake Island [4] — before the emotional center of the speech: the vow that the American people \"in their righteous might will win through to absolute victory\" [5].\n\nThe actual request is a single sentence at the end: that Congress declare that a state of war has existed since the attack [6].","citations":[{"quote":"yesterday, December 7th, 1941, a date which will live in infamy.","wi":14,"wj":25,"s":11.14,"e":24.12,"corrob":0.9091},{"quote":"It will be recorded that the distance of Hawaii from Japan makes it obvious that the attack was deliberately planned many days or even weeks ago.","wi":146,"wj":172,"s":105.72,"e":122.48,"corrob":1},{"quote":"the Japanese government has deliberately sought to deceive the United States by false statements and expressions of hope for continued peace.","wi":176,"wj":197,"s":125.58,"e":139.5,"corrob":1},{"quote":"Last night, Japanese forces attacked Hong Kong. Last night, Japanese forces attacked Guam.","wi":260,"wj":273,"s":177.98,"e":188.1,"corrob":1},{"quote":"the American people, in their righteous might, will win through to absolute victory.","wi":379,"wj":392,"s":275.68,"e":283.28,"corrob":1},{"quote":"I ask that the Congress declare that since the unprovoked and dastardly attack by Japan on Sunday, December 7th, 1941, a state of war has existed between the United States and the Japanese Empire.","wi":485,"wj":519,"s":382.56,"e":412.02,"corrob":0.9706}]},"chapters":[{"title":"A date which will live in infamy","at":{"quote":"yesterday, December 7th, 1941, a date which will live in infamy.","wi":14,"wj":25,"s":11.14,"e":24.12,"corrob":0.9091}},{"title":"The deception","at":{"quote":"Indeed, one hour after Japanese air squadrons had commenced bombing in the American island","wi":79,"wj":93,"s":58.54,"e":68.02,"corrob":1}},{"title":"The Pacific-wide offensive","at":{"quote":"Yesterday, the Japanese government also launched an attack against Malaya.","wi":250,"wj":260,"s":169.38,"e":177.44,"corrob":1}},{"title":"The vow","at":{"quote":"No matter how long it may take us to overcome this premeditated invasion, the American people, in their righteous might, will win through to absolute victory.","wi":366,"wj":392,"s":268.08,"e":283.28,"corrob":1}},{"title":"The declaration of war","at":{"quote":"I ask that the Congress declare that since the unprovoked and dastardly attack by Japan","wi":485,"wj":500,"s":382.56,"e":395.4,"corrob":1}}],"concepts":[{"term":"Infamy","definition":"The word the speech is remembered by. Roosevelt's drafts said \"a date which will live in world history\"; the delivered word turns a date into a verdict.","cite":{"quote":"yesterday, December 7th, 1941, a date which will live in infamy.","wi":14,"wj":25,"s":11.14,"e":24.12,"corrob":0.9091}},{"term":"Premeditation","definition":"The load-bearing argument: geography as evidence. If Hawaii is that far from Japan, the attack fleet sailed while the peace negotiations were still running.","cite":{"quote":"makes it obvious that the attack was deliberately planned many days or even weeks ago.","wi":157,"wj":172,"s":112.98,"e":122.48,"corrob":1}},{"term":"Anaphora (\"Last night…\")","definition":"The repeated sentence-opener is the speech's engineering: each strike gets its own sentence, so the scale of the offensive accumulates blow by blow instead of arriving as a list.","cite":{"quote":"Last night, Japanese forces attacked Guam. Last night, Japanese forces attacked the Philippine island.","wi":267,"wj":281,"s":183.66,"e":194.08,"corrob":0.963}}],"flags":[]},"notes":[{"id":"fdr-infamy_c0","kind":"quote","text":"yesterday, December 7th, 1941, a date which will live in infamy.","quote":"yesterday, December 7th, 1941, a date which will live in infamy.","anchor":{"s":11.14,"e":24.12,"wi":14,"wj":25,"quality":"word"},"heard":false,"createdAt":1787443200000,"updatedAt":1787443200000},{"id":"fdr-infamy_c2","kind":"quote","text":"we will not only defend ourselves to the uttermost, but will make it very certain that this form of treachery shall never again endanger us.","quote":"we will not only defend ourselves to the uttermost, but will make it very certain that this form of treachery shall never again endanger us.","anchor":{"s":318.86,"e":333.08,"wi":410,"wj":435,"quality":"word"},"heard":false,"createdAt":1787443200000,"updatedAt":1787443200000},{"id":"fdr-infamy_c1","kind":"point","text":"The whole request is one sentence at the very end — everything before it is evidence.","quote":"I ask that the Congress declare that since the unprovoked and dastardly attack by Japan","anchor":{"s":382.56,"e":395.4,"wi":485,"wj":500,"quality":"word"},"heard":false,"createdAt":1787443200000,"updatedAt":1787443200000}],"peaks":[0.582,0.496,0.557,0.562,0.498,0.617,0.748,0.721,0.629,0.808,0.786,0.601,0.591,0.796,0.669,0.595,0.764,0.704,0.661,0.559,0.857,0.768,0.729,0.826,0.731,0.629,0.695,0.563,0.767,0.436,0.836,0.889,0.756,0.826,0.577,0.667,0.671,0.626,0.552,0.756,0.803,0.832,0.776,0.568,0.7,0.782,0.719,0.658,0.527,0.545,0.647,0.678,0.621,0.755,0.522,0.894,0.676,0.722,0.554,0.832,0.628,0.598,0.634,0.677,0.568,0.718,0.549,0.605,0.609,0.782,0.593,0.829,0.652,0.786,0.313,0.579,0.667,0.765,0.956,0.81,0.746,0.685,0.456,0.717,0.801,0.673,0.803,0.619,0.669,0.346,0.572,0.511,0.583,0.683,0.806,0.73,0.767,0.959,0.599,0.598,0.577,0.5,0.495,0.609,0.727,0.669,0.359,0.59,0.599,0.535,0.767,0.673,0.661,0.646,0.691,0.781,0.654,0.422,0